 "fingerprint_sd_note": "PINNED. The standard deviations of the five numeric fingerprint dimensions across the shipped 87-weapon roster, measured once and frozen here so that build-movesets.mjs is a PURE FUNCTION of its inputs. An earlier version read them back from the previous build's output, which made the generator a feedback loop with a 2-cycle: six weapon files alternated between two states on successive runs and `--check` reported drift forever. game/data/weapons/fp-sd.json is still written on every build as a REPORT, so if the roster changes enough for these to be wrong it is visible in a diff.",
 "haft_damage_mult_note": "S26 contiguity, W1-10 round 3. `hitbox_span_m` is the EDGED span of the weapon. Wave 1 spent it by starting the hit capsule at `capsule_length - hitbox_span_m`, which put an interior hole in eleven weapons' reachable bands (a spear could not hit a man at 1.4 m) and left five classes unable to hit a target standing against them. The capsule now runs from the grip to the tip and is contiguous by construction; `hitbox_span_m` is consumed instead as the point beyond which the weapon is edged, and a contact INBOARD of it deals `haft_damage_mult` of the blow. That keeps the design fact the span column was written for -- an axe hurts at the head and a sword hurts along its length -- as a damage fact rather than as a geometry hole. Consumed at game/src/combat/resolve.js, and perturbing any of these fifteen values changes the damage of a close-in hit: tools/weapons/impact-consumption.mjs proves it."
}
